| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `src/store/chats.js` | Modify | `actions` → `startChatProcessing` | New named action that flags a chat as processing immediately (wraps existing `setChatUpdating` mutation, which schedules the 10s auto-reset timeout used as the "server didn't respond" safety net). |
| `src/components/chat/Chat.vue` | Modify | `computed` → `isProcessing` | New computed exposing the shared `isChatUpdating(chat.id)` store flag. |
| `src/components/chat/Chat.vue` | Modify | `methods` → `sendChatMessage` | Calls `$chats.startChatProcessing({ chatId })` right after `waiting = true`, so processing is registered the instant the user sends (before the socket `await`). |
| `src/components/chat/Chat.vue` | Modify | `<ChatMessageList>` | Passes `:processing="isProcessing"` down to the message list. |
| `src/components/chat/ChatMessageList.vue` | Modify | `props` | Adds `processing` prop. |
| `src/components/chat/ChatMessageList.vue` | Modify | `computed` | Adds `hasStreamingAssistantMessage` and `showProcessingPlaceholder` (hides placeholder once the real assistant bubble starts streaming). |
| `src/components/chat/ChatMessageList.vue` | Modify | `template` | Adds an accessible (`role="status"`, `aria-live="polite"`) "Assistant is working…" placeholder bubble with animated dots at the end of the conversation. |

### Notes / Behaviour
- The indicator appears **synchronously on click** and is cleared either by the server's first `done` event (`onChatEvent → setChatUpdating(false)`) or by the store's **10s timeout**, which covers a non-responsive server.
- Once the real assistant message begins streaming, its existing progress bar/skeleton takes over and the placeholder hides — no double indicator.
- The same flag also drives the kanban tree, subtask cards and the desktop tab icon ring, so those now light up immediately too (consistent feedback).

